# The Shelf — front-end configuration.
#
# These two values are PUBLIC BY DESIGN and are deliberately committed. They
# are compiled into the JavaScript bundle, so anyone using the app can read
# them; hiding them would be theatre, not security.
#
# What actually protects the collection is that this key has no privileges:
#   * every table's grants were REVOKED from the anon role, and
#   * no row-level-security policy grants anon anything.
# Confirmed by test — querying films with this key returns Postgres error
# 42501, "permission denied", even though the table holds 248 rows.
#
# The keys that ARE secret (TMDB_KEY, DTDD_KEY, the Supabase service-role key)
# live only as Edge Function secrets and in the Supabase CLI. None of them
# belongs in this file, this repo, or the browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://agqheazstgzyvjglxjad.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImFncWhlYXpzdGd6eXZqZ2x4amFkIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODg1ODgwNTgsImV4cCI6MjEwNDE2NDA1OH0.JMU03dBsGW19zGtcwOcb_8pQEsBU9ppPv4JILJmNO1c
